.\" trash-rm(1) manual page for trash-cli.
.TH TRASH-RM 1 2026-11-14 "trash-cli 0.26.9.29" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
trash\-rm \- remove individual files from the trash can
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B trash\-rm \fIPATTERN\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B trash\-rm
removes entries from the trash cans by pattern: for every matching
trashinfo file, the backup copy in
.I files/
is removed first (if present, dangling symlinks included), then the info
file itself.
Entries of
.I files/
without an info file are never touched.
Success is completely silent, whether zero or several entries matched.
.PP
There are no options:
\fB\-\-help\fR
and
\fB\-\-version\fR
do not exist, they are patterns.
Extra arguments are silently ignored.
With no argument a usage block is printed to standard error and the exit
status is 8:
.RS
.PP
.nf
Usage:
    trash\-rm PATTERN

Please specify PATTERN.
trash\-rm uses fnmatch.fnmatchcase to match patterns, see https://docs.python.org/3/library/fnmatch.html for more details.
.fi
.RE
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I PATTERN
A fnmatch(3) pattern, matched case\-sensitively everywhere
(\fBfnmatchcase\fR
semantics):
\fB*\fR
matches any string including
\fB/\fR,
\fB?\fR
matches one character, and
\fB[seq]\fR
and
\fB[!seq]\fR
are character classes.
A
.I PATTERN
starting with
\fB/\fR
is matched against the full original location; any other
.I PATTERN
is matched against the basename only, so a pattern with a
\fB/\fR
in a non\-leading position never matches.
An empty
.I PATTERN
matches nothing and the exit status is 0.
.SH TRASH DIRECTORIES
The trash cans scanned are the home trash,
\fI$XDG_DATA_HOME/Trash\fR
when
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
is set and non\-empty and
\fI$HOME/.local/share/Trash\fR
otherwise, followed by, for every volume
\fI$volume\fR,
\fI$volume\fB/.Trash/\fI$uid\fR
(trust\-checked, silently skipped when the checks fail) and
\fI$volume\fB/.Trash\-\fI$uid\fR.
\fBTRASH_VOLUMES\fR
is honored, as in
.BR trash\-list (1).
.PP
A trashinfo file that cannot be parsed is reported on standard error as
\fBtrash\-rm: \fI<info path>\fB: unable to parse \(aqPath\(aq\fR
and skipped; the scan continues.
An entry that is not valid UTF\-8 is reported as
\fBtrash\-rm: \fI<info path>\fB: unable to parse trashinfo (invalid UTF\-8)\fR
and skipped the same way.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, including a pattern that matched nothing and an empty pattern.
.TP
.B 8
No pattern given.
.TP
.B 1
Fatal error.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Location of the home trash,
\fI$XDG_DATA_HOME/Trash\fR.
Used only when set and non\-empty; an empty value is treated as unset, per
the XDG basedir specification, so the home trash falls back to
\fI$HOME/.local/share/Trash\fR.
A relative value is used verbatim, resolved against the current directory.
.TP
.B HOME
Fallback location of the home trash,
\fI$HOME/.local/share/Trash\fR.
.TP
.B TRASH_VOLUMES
Colon\-separated volume list overriding the mount table; empty items are
dropped.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/Trash
The home trash, when
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
is set and non\-empty.
.TP
.I $HOME/.local/share/Trash
The home trash otherwise.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.PP
.nf
trash\-rm notes.txt
trash\-rm *.o
trash\-rm /home/user/work/scratch*
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR trash\-put (1),
.BR trash (1),
.BR trash\-list (1),
.BR trash\-restore (1),
.BR trash\-empty (1),
.BR fnmatch (3).
.PP
Implements the FreeDesktop.org Trash Specification,
https://specifications.freedesktop.org/trash\-spec/
